{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1508216-protectorate-totems","id":1508216,"title":"Protectorate Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-12T17:03:22-07:00","id":1508216,"title":"Protectorate Totems","content":"Browsing the forums today after work, Cappelletti and Acqua Panna glassed beside my left hand, bedroom window open to the spring breeze and starlingcalls, I came across an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1508066-finding-the-tiers-in-cofd\">interesting thread</a> about functioning tiers in Chronicles games. As per my usual habit of dreaming up a response that I never actually post, I started musing a bit on the relationship Forsaken has to tiers, mainly settling on the phrase &quot;Werewolf's intentionally messy intersections between Pack, Lodge, Tribe, and Protectorate.&quot; I smiled, took a sip of my drink, and did not click Post. Then it dawned on me: Out of these four socio-politico-spiritual groupings in Forsaken, only the last one is devoid of any totemic empowerment. It's fitting, since Protectorates are in a way the most <i>human</i> kind of organization the Uratha are inclined to create, but also curious. Certainly the <i>Hisil</i>'s denizens might take an interest in what the wolves are getting up to, organizing territory on a larger-than-natural scale, packs working together to accomplish goals none could complete alone (a <i>pack-of-packs</i> if you will). There's power there: Power to fear, and power to covet. Maybe some spirit that knows what's up would reach out an ephemeral tendril an offer a deal. After all, what's one more bit of spiritual scarification on top of all the others the Uratha put themselves through?<br /> <br /> So, now I am thinking: What sorts of spirits might be interested in becoming totems to Protectorates? The kinds with bigger dreams than pack totems, doubtlessly. Ones with goals that can't be accomplished through Lodges as well. So the ideal spirit is both powerful and intimately local. The incarnations of Protectorates' very territories spring to mind: Perhaps all the Forsaken of Savannah bend a knee to The Pretty Lady With A Dirty Face from time to time. Maybe at that level of political power you're drawing the interest of those weird and eerie spirit nobles, with their obelisks and masks and plans-within-plans. It's a Faustian bargain, but one with a high payoff, potentially. If you don't get screwed over.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what do you think Protectorate totems would look like? What sorts of powers and privileges would they grant their constituents? What expectations and bans would they levy? What webs might they be weaving for these presumptuous little wolves who obviously didn't learn their lesson back in Sumer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T17:47:10-07:00","id":1508220,"title":"","content":"Likely? Regional spirits like the spirit of a given city or bit of countryside.<br /> <br /> Whatever brings a protectorate together is usually something highly disruptive to the local ecosystem and possibly could even permanently damage the cycles of feast, famine, and replenishment in the food chains, and as the harmonious consumer of all their elements, that's not something that's gonna fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:50:09-07:00","id":1508244,"title":"","content":"IMO. A protectorate spirit is probably only going to get the same returns on essence as a spirit over a small lodge, so probably about 1 essence a day. Enough to live on but not enough for more than that. I know I don't want to work 24/7 just to eat. (This is all based on vague memories of lodge spirits getting 1-5 / day.)<br /> <br /> So that makes me think a spirit over a protectorate has to be gaining more than just essence. A spirit of unity or cooperation might work. A regional spirit might work. They would all have things to gain besides the just the essence. <br /> <br /> There are other options though. A magath, for example, might find itself in desperate need of friends and protection after it's creation. Or maybe some spirit offended the local court and would like not to be eaten. <br /> <br /> There is still another option though. Uratha are hunters. Strong and mighty and scary as fuck hunters. They very well might have found a spirit and made it an offer it couldn't refuse. We're werewolves, not saints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}